{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "title": "WebToServer",
  "description": "Messages sent from web client to server",
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "description": "Authenticate with JWT token",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "app_version": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "capabilities": {
          "type": "array",
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "client_kind": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/ClientKind"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "protocol_version": {
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "token": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "authenticate"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "token"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "List available CLI clients",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "list_cli_clients"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "List daemon-reported machines and projects for this user",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "list_machines"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Start a new session (optionally specify CLI client)",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "cli_client_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "start_session"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Resume an existing session",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "resume_session"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "session_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Attach to observe an existing CLI session (hybrid mode)",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "attach_session"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "session_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "User input to send to Claude.\nWhen `session_id` is set, the server routes to that exact session\n(after verifying this web connection is attached to it). This is the\nonly safe option for clients that multi-attach: the connection's\nlast-attached session is non-deterministic when several attaches\nrace. Omitted = legacy single-attach behaviour.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "client_msg_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "pane_id": {
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "pane_type": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/PaneType"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "input"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "text"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "A deliberate chat-style message for a terminal-hosted agent. Unlike\n[`WebToServer::TerminalInput`], this is safe to persist and display in\nconversation history because the user submitted it through the\nconversation composer rather than typing arbitrary terminal bytes.\nThe server converts it to terminal input and appends Enter.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "client_msg_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "pane_id": {
          "type": "integer",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "terminal_conversation_input"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "session_id",
        "pane_id",
        "text"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Approve a tool call. See `Input::session_id` for the multi-attach rationale.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "pane_id": {
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "request_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "tool_call_id": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "approve"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "tool_call_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Reject a tool call. See `Input::session_id`.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "pane_id": {
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "request_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "tool_call_id": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "reject"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "tool_call_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Send signal (e.g., cancel/interrupt). See `Input::session_id`.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "signal": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "signal"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "signal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "List all sessions (persisted)",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "list_sessions"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Get messages for a specific session (with optional pagination)",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "after_created_at": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "before_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "limit": {
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uint",
          "default": null,
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "pane_id": {
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "pane_type": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/PaneType"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "pane_watermarks": {
          "type": [
            "object",
            "null"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "get_session_messages"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "session_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Pause the deadloop session (legacy - use PausePane for new code)",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "pause_deadloop"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Resume the deadloop session (legacy - use ResumePane for new code)",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "resume_deadloop"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Pause a specific pane. See `Input::session_id`.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "pane_id": {
          "type": "integer",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "pause_pane"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "pane_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Resume a specific pane. See `Input::session_id`.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "pane_id": {
          "type": "integer",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "resume_pane"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "pane_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Soft-restart a single pane's agent on its existing session when\npossible (see `ServerToCli::RebootPane`).",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "pane_id": {
          "type": "integer",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "reboot_pane"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "pane_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Add a new pane",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "backstory": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "goal": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "isolated_worktree": {
          "description": "When true, the CLI creates an isolated git worktree under\n`<project>/.apas-worktrees/pane-<id>` (branch `apas-pane-<id>`)\nbefore spawning, and persists the resulting absolute path on\nPaneConfig.worktree_path. Phase 1.1e.",
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false
        },
        "kind": {
          "description": "Agent (default) vs Terminal. A Terminal pane ignores `prompt`,\n`role`, `goal`, `backstory` and `plan_review_mode` — there is\nno system prompt to inject into a pty-hosted TUI.",
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PaneKind",
          "default": "agent"
        },
        "label": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "managed": {
          "description": "v3.5 — true when this pane is being added as part of the\nproject team, false for ordinary user-created terminal work. See\nPaneConfig::managed.",
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false
        },
        "mode": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PaneMode"
        },
        "model": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "plan_review_mode": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PlanReviewMode",
          "default": "never"
        },
        "prompt": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "provider": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Provider"
        },
        "role": {
          "description": "Initial role/goal/backstory/plan_review_mode applied to the new\npane BEFORE the first spawn — so a templated worker (Add Worker\nmodal on Overview) uses the right system prompt immediately\ninstead of needing a close+reopen. All optional; missing fields\nkeep the legacy \"set via Role modal later\" path.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "add_pane"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "provider",
        "mode"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Remove a pane. When the pane has an isolated worktree assigned\n(`PaneConfig.worktree_path` set), `cleanup_action` says what to do\nwith that worktree and its branch. None = leave the on-disk worktree\nand branch alone (legacy behaviour — just unlink the pane from .apas).",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "cleanup_action": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/PaneCleanupAction"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "pane_id": {
          "type": "integer",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "remove_pane"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "pane_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Update a pane's custom label",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "label": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "pane_id": {
          "type": "integer",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "update_pane_label"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "pane_id",
        "label"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Update a pane's Claude thinking-effort override. Persisted in the\nproject .apas so switching tabs doesn't reset it to default.\n`session_id` is optional (see `InterruptPane`): when present the server\nvalidates/auto-attaches this connection to that session, so the change\nisn't misrouted to the connection's drifting last-attached session\n(which breaks the mobile fan-out); absent = legacy connection-session.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "effort": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "pane_id": {
          "type": "integer",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid",
          "default": null
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "update_pane_effort"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "pane_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Switch a pane's agent backend (provider + model). The CLI kills\nthe current agent child and respawns with a fresh session id —\nthe new agent starts with no prior chat context. See\n`ServerToCli::UpdatePaneModel` for the full semantics.\n`session_id` is optional (see `InterruptPane`): when present the server\nvalidates/auto-attaches this connection to that session, so the switch\nisn't misrouted to the connection's drifting last-attached session\n(which broke the model selector on mobile); absent = legacy behavior.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "model": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "pane_id": {
          "type": "integer",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "provider": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Provider"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid",
          "default": null
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "update_pane_model"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "pane_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Interrupt the agent process running for a pane (e.g. claude wedged on\na long-running Bash tool call). The CLI signals SIGINT to its\nsubprocess so the current turn aborts and queued input can flow.\n`session_id` is optional for backward compat: when present the server\nvalidates/auto-attaches the connection to that session (so \"Stop team\"\ninterrupts survive a just-reconnected connection); when absent it falls\nback to the connection's currently-attached session.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "pane_id": {
          "type": "integer",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "request_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid",
          "default": null
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "interrupt_pane"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "pane_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Reorder panes (array of pane_ids in desired order)",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "pane_ids": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "integer",
            "format": "uint32",
            "minimum": 0
          }
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "reorder_panes"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "pane_ids"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Start bot (deadloop) on a pane — converts interactive pane to deadloop",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "effort": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "min_iteration_interval_minutes": {
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uint64",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "pane_id": {
          "type": "integer",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "prompt": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "start_bot"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "pane_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Stop bot on a pane — converts deadloop pane back to interactive",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "pane_id": {
          "type": "integer",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "stop_bot"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "pane_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Reboot the CLI process",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "reboot_cli"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Capability-gated project lifecycle operation. `session_id` is\nrequired so multi-attached web connections cannot accidentally target\nthe last session that happened to attach.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "operation": {
          "description": "`None` when the client asked for an operation this build retired.",
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/CliLifecycleOperation"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "request_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "cli_lifecycle_request"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "session_id",
        "request_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Start APAS CLI for a daemon project",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "machine_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "project_id": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "start_machine_project_cli"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "machine_id",
        "project_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Stop APAS CLI for a daemon project",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "machine_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "project_id": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "stop_machine_project_cli"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "machine_id",
        "project_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Restart the daemon on one machine, applying an available update first.\n\nTargeted by machine rather than by a project on it: a daemon is\nper-machine, and a machine running nothing has no project to route\nthrough. Restarting a daemon does not disturb the projects, panes, or\nagents on that host — the daemon owns no long-lived children.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "machine_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "uuid"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "reboot_daemon"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "machine_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Create a brand-new project instance under a repo on a chosen machine:\nthe daemon clones `clone_url` into `~/apas_projects/<instance_name>`\n(auto-suffixed on collision), checks out a fresh `branch`, registers a\n`.apas`, and starts it. `git_remote` is the canonical key (for the\ndaemon's sibling-URL fallback + naming); `clone_url` is the real URL.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "base_path": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "branch": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "clone_url": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "git_remote": {
          "type": "string"
        },
